    "title": "Wisconsin basketball vs. High Point TV channel, tip time revealed",
    "text": "March 16, 2026, 5:20 a.m. CTThe No. 5-seed Wisconsin Badgers are set to travel to Portland, Oregon, for a first-round NCAA Tournament matchup against No. 12 High Point.Shortly after Selection Sunday, the tip times, TV channel, and announcing crew was revealed for the Badgers game.Wisconsin is set to have a 1:50 p.m. ET tipoff on TBS. Remember, they are among the first teams to play this year with an afternoon tip-off on Thursday, March 19. Should Wisconsin win, it will be back in action on Saturday, March 21. Looking at the team's opponent, though, that's far from a guarantee.Brad Nessler, Wally Szczerbiak, and Jared Greenberg will be on the call for the first game of the day in Portland.No. 4 Arkansas vs. No. 13 Hawaii will follow, with an expected tipoff time of 4:25 p.m. ET, though that's obviously dependent on how quickly things go in the Badgers game.Wisconsin has only twice lost in the first round of the NCAA Tournament in its last eight seasons. Granted, the team missed the tournament entirely in two of those seasons, and another was cancelled due to COVID-19. Either way, this is an incredible team Greg Gard has put together, and now it's time to show the world what the 2025-26 Badgers are truly made of.Contact/Follow@TheBadgersWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page onFacebook to follow ongoing coverage of WisconsinBadgers news, notes and opinion.",
